course: dictionary
lesson: 820
title: Believe and belief
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word believe has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one fits. To believe something means to think it is true. «Wait for trusted news before believing or sharing that a famous person has died» means you should check first, not just accept what you read.
explain: To believe someone means to trust that they are telling the truth. «Laugh at the advert's trick, not at the person who believed it» shows that people can be tricked into believing something false. The clue is the trick: the person thought it was true, and it was not.
explain: Sometimes «I believe» means «I think, but I am not completely sure». To check, swap in think: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. The noun belief is the thing you hold to be true.
fact: Believe is a verb, and its other forms are believes, believed and believing; the noun is belief.
fact: To believe something means to think it is true; to believe someone means to trust that they are telling the truth.
fact: To believe in something means to feel sure it exists or is good, as in believing in yourself.
fact: «I believe» can mean «I think, but I am not completely sure».
fact: Good science checks evidence: we test and check, rather than just believing what someone says.
exercise: «A miracle is an amazing event that Christians believe shows God's power at work.» What does believe mean here? | To trust a person who is telling the truth | *To think it is true | To wear a hat | To be very tired
exercise: «Laugh at the advert's trick, not at the person who believed it.» What does believed mean here? | *Thought the trick was true | Forgot the trick | Told the trick to a friend | Laughed at the trick
exercise: «Don't believe a stranger who says your parent sent them unless they know the family password.» What does believe mean here? | Remember them later | Think they are a nice person | Feel sure they are tall | *Trust that they are telling the truth
test: Which word is the noun form of believe? | believing | believed | believes | *belief
test: Ellie says, «I believe it will snow, but I am not completely sure.» What does I believe mean? | *I think, but I am not completely sure | I know for certain | I have been told to stay inside | I have proof it will snow
exam: What does «make-believe» describe? | Something proven by tests | A person who is always honest | A loud noise in the street | *Something pretended or imagined
